          "nature": "warm",
          "flavor": "acrid, slightly bitter",
          "meridians": [
            "Lung channel",
            "Bladder channel"
          ],
          "dosage": "Internal decoction 1.5–10 g; external: appropriate amount (powder for nasal insufflation or topical); raw and honey-fried preparations differ in strength",
          "preparation_method": "Raw: cut into sections and dry. Honey-fried: stir-fry with cooked refined honey (per 100 jin herb use 10–15 jin honey). Raw has strong diaphoretic power; honey-frying reduces diaphoretic power and moistens the Lung, stopping cough and calming wheezing.",
          "contraindications": "Contraindicated in constitutionally weak individuals with spontaneous sweating, night sweats, or chronic asthma; contraindicated in exterior deficiency with spontaneous sweating, yin deficiency with night sweating, lung deficiency with heat and copious phlegm causing nasal obstruction, and other debilitated states as described in classical sources."
